 "observations": [
  "The page number «216» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the left the number of the table, «Tab. 101», in bold sans serif, underlined. The page has no signature and no title: the folios of the manuscripts stand at the left above the double rule of the first field, in one line of their own, «C 95v, O 151r, N 62r.», the letters raised (L01).",
  "The page holds three fields, as pp. 206-215 (JP2 0238-0247): «Quinque1) gradus Virginis» (L02), «Decem2) gradus Virginis» (L14) and «Quindecim3) gradus Virginis» (L22), the ascendant at 5°, 10° and 15° of Virgo, with the numbers for the sextile, the quadrature and the trine (L03, L15, L23); headings and numbers in bold; in L15 «69°32′» without the space after the sign of the degrees. The columns begin with the sign of the ascendant: «Virgo Pisces Horoscopus», «Libra Aries Horoscopus», «Scorpius Taurus Horoscopus», «Sagittar. Gemini Horoscopus», «Capricorn. Cancer Horoscopus» and «Aquarius Leo Horoscopus», without notes; here each head is set from the top, one printed line to a line (L04-L06), with «Gradus aequales», printed upwards, in L04-L05, and the units in L07. The numbers are counted from the beginning of Virgo. The second and the third field have no heads. Double rules divide the fields.",
  "The numbers at the head of a field, as on pp. 206-215 (JP2 0238-0247), are a third, a half and two thirds of the last number of the field: 208° 26′ (L13) gives 69° 28.7′, 104° 13′ and 138° 57.3′, printed 69° 29′, 104° 13′ and 138° 57′ (L03); 208° 37′ (L21) gives 69° 32.3′, 104° 18.5′ and 139° 4.7′, printed 69° 32′, 104° 18′ and 139° 5′ (L15); 208° 57′ (L29) gives 69° 39′, 104° 28.5′ and 139° 18′, printed 69° 39′, 104° 28′ and 139° 18′ (L23). The last numbers of the fields of Virgo, 208° 26′, 208° 37′ and 208° 57′, lie within 31′ of one another and 26′ to 57′ above the 208° 0′ of the last field of Leo (p. 215, JP2 0247, L29).",
  "The columns: in Virgo the three fields lie within 24′, 16′ and 31′ of the oblique ascensions from the beginning of Virgo for the latitude 38° 30′ (computed with the obliquity 23° 35′; 6° 15′, 12° 28′, 18° 41′, 24° 52′, 31° 3′, 37° 14′); from Libra on they fall below them, by 8° 22′, 7° 21′ and 6° 34′ at the end of Sagittarius (139° 11′, 140° 12′ and 140° 59′ for 147° 33′). In Capricornus and Aquarius, the signs of short ascension, the oblique ascensions grow more slowly than the columns, which pass them between 5° and 10° of Aquarius and end 9° 44′, 9° 55′ and 10° 15′ above them (208° 26′, 208° 37′ and 208° 57′ for 198° 42′).",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the other fields, which differ by 5° of the ascendant, and by the steps of the columns: the edition's readings are the nearer at 5° of Scorpius in the first field (note a, L08: O's 78 against C's 68), at 30° of Aquarius in the first (note b, L13: the editor's 208 for the 201 of all three manuscripts; the numbers at the head belong to 208° 26′ to 208° 27′), at 10° of Virgo in the second (note c, L17: C's 30 against O's 35, the steps 6° 20′ and 6° 15′ against 6° 25′ and 6° 10′; the oblique ascension 12° 28.5′), at 10° of Scorpius in the second (note d, L17: C's 84 against O's 88), at 20° and 25° of Capricornus in the second (notes e and f, L19-L20: the editor's 162 and 167 for the 192 and 197 of the manuscripts), at 30° of Virgo in the third (note g, L29: C's 36 against O's 37, the steps 6° 8′ and 6° 0′ into Libra against 7° 8′ and 5° 0′; the column of Virgo rises by 6° 10′ in each of the first four steps), at 15° and 20° of Virgo in the third (notes h and i, L26-L27: the minutes of N, 30 and 40, which C and O omit) and at 25° of Aquarius in the third (note k, L28: the 203 of O and N against C's 103).",
  "Without variants: the editor's 162° 41′ at 20° of Capricornus in the second field (note e, L19) lies 5′ above the third field (162° 36′, L27), where the second field lies 34′ to 50′ below the third from 5° to 15° and from 25° to 30° of Capricornus, between the steps 6° 14′ and 4° 51′. In the first field the column of Sagittarius rises by 5° 25′, 5° 5′, 4° 50′, 6° 10′, 5° 18′ and 5° 31′ (L08-L13).",
  "In the head «Horoscopus» over Capricornus and Cancer (L06) the H is damaged, its left stem broken at the top, and a speck stands over the second o; not transcribed. Italics: «om.»."
